{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract qc relate [-h] [--sites SITES] [--ped PED] [--ancestry | --no-ancestry]\n                            [--format {tsv,parquet}]\n                            FILE [FILE ...]\n\npositional arguments:\n  FILE                  BAM, CRAM or VCF files, or .somalier sketches from an earlier run.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --sites SITES         Sites VCF to genotype instead of somalier's own for the input's build\n                        (default: from 'ref somalier --install').\n  --ped PED             PED/FAM file of the expected relationships and sexes; pairs or sexes that\n                        disagree are flagged as possible sample swaps.\n  --ancestry, --no-ancestry\n                        Predict the 1000 Genomes superpopulation (default: when 'ref somalier\n                        --install' has installed the labelled sketches).\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Table format: tsv, or parquet (needs pyarrow) (default: tsv)\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract qc relate me.cram\n  wgsextract qc relate child.cram mother.cram father.cram --ped trio.ped\n  wgsextract qc relate me.cram somalier/cousin.somalier --no-ancestry\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  relate.samples.tsv (sex, superpopulation), relate.pairs.tsv (relatedness),\n  relate.html and the sketches in somalier/, in --outdir, else beside the\n  first input.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, samtools, somalier; depending on options and inputs, also: bgzip,\n  tabix; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
